<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marquis de Tracy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1596–<a href="/years/1670">1670</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Alexandre de Prouville de Tracy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexandre de Prouville, Marquis de Tracy, was a French soldier sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> as lieutenant general for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s American colonies. He reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> in 1665 with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carignan-salieres-regiment">Carignan-Salières Regiment</a>, the first large body of regular troops in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>, and built forts along the Richelieu River. In 1666 he led an expedition that burned the Mohawk villages and their food stores, forcing the Mohawk to make peace in 1667.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marquis-de-tracy.jpg" alt="Marquis de Tracy" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexandre_de_Prouville_de_Tracy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
